      "Measured by landing its own claim by rebase with two commits - the host names the later commit, and the wait found the push run on it",
      "Executor was a Sonnet subagent; the fresh-agent check was run by the author on Opus 5.5 and did not exercise the dispatch and refresh-board wording",
      "One fix made in review and declared - a test that pins the workflow statements six criteria rest on; decision recorded as FW-076"
    ],
    "stage-jobs-restore-npm-from-a-cache": [
      "Narrowed criterion 1 - the plan, host and gate jobs install nothing and leave the cache off, so the first job does not save an empty cache the stages would then restore",
      "Executor ran as a subagent on Sonnet - the Small pick dispatch named runs in Cursor, which a cloud session cannot start",
      "Parent review, not self-merge; no decision record, the reasons are in comments in the workflow file",
      "Not yet seen on a real run - to confirm on the first pipeline run after a release carrying it is installed, with three behaviours of the cache settings that could not be checked against the host's documentation"
